{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"stem"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStem","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLStemV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLStem"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML "},{"code":"<stem>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}]}]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The direction of the stem for this note, if any."}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"stem"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLStemV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLStem"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"title":"stem","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Property","symbolKind":"property","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLNoteV4stemAA7MXLStemVSgvp"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/stem"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/stem","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStem":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Stems can be down, up, none, or double. For down and up stems, the position attributes can be used to specify"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stem length. The relative values specify the end of the stem relative to the program default. Default values"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specify an absolute end stem position. Negative values of relative-y that would flip a stem instead of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shortening it are ignored. A stem element associated with a rest refers to a stemlet."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLStem"}],"title":"MXLStem","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLStem"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstem","type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStem"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote","title":"MXLNote","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNote","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNote","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Notes are the most common type of MusicXML data. The MusicXML format distinguishes between elements used for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sound information and elements used for notation information (e.g., tie is used for sound, tied for notation)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Thus grace notes do not have a duration element. Cue notes have a duration element, as do forward elements,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"but no tie elements. Having these two types of information available can make interchange easier, as some","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"programs handle one type of information more readily than the other."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote/stem":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/stem","role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/stem","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The direction of the stem for this note, if any."}],"title":"stem","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"stem","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLStemV","text":"MXLStem","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"}}}